---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import IntakeForm from '../components/IntakeForm.astro';
import HeroBanner from '../components/HeroBanner.astro';
import FamilyClusterNav from '../components/FamilyClusterNav.astro';
import RequirementsIntakeCta from '../components/RequirementsIntakeCta.astro';

const title = 'Portugal HQA Visa Family - Spouse and Children Coverage';
const metaTitle = `${title} | Portugal HQA Residency`;
const metaDescription =
  'Portugal HQA visa family coverage in 2026 is spouse and children on the principal file, not automatic cards. Open this hub, then the two supporting pages.';
---

<Layout title={metaTitle} description={metaDescription}>
  <article>
    <header>
      <HeroBanner
        image="/images/portugal-hqa-visa-family-together.jpg"
        alt="White courtyard walls in cooler light, with dark doorways opening onto grass under a blue sky"
        title={title}
        items={[
          { href: '/', label: 'Home' },
          { href: '/portugal-hqa-visa', label: 'Portugal HQA Visa' },
          { label: 'Family' },
        ]}
      />
      <div class="bg-background">
        <div class="site-container py-24 md:py-32">
        <p class="max-w-3xl">
          Portugal HQA visa family coverage allows the spouse and dependent children of a principal applicant to obtain residence in Portugal through family reunification. Family members are not included automatically and must submit their own applications with the required identity, relationship, and, where applicable, financial support documentation.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl">
          The principal applicant must first qualify under the
          <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-requirements" class="inline-link">HQA visa requirements</a>.
          Each family member then holds their own residence status, and eligibility for
          <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-permanent-residency" class="inline-link">HQA visa permanent residency</a>
          is assessed separately for each residence permit holder.
        </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="bg-background-alt">
      <div class="site-container py-24 md:py-32">
        <div class="max-w-3xl">
          <section>
            <h2>Family members are not a second principal</h2>
            <p class="mt-6">
              The highly qualified activity test applies to the worker or hosted researcher. A spouse does not become eligible by marriage alone. A child does not become eligible by travelling on the same flight. Each included person receives their own residence analysis and, if granted, their own card. Timing can be with the principal’s first lodging or in a later family filing. The post decides which window is open.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-4">
              This hub does not reprint the document checklist or the lodging steps. It points to who in the household can be covered, then to the two pages that own spouse and children.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <RequirementsIntakeCta
      source="/portugal-hqa-visa-family"
      image="/images/portugal-hqa-visa-family-cta-divider.jpg"
      alt="Lisbon family-scale neighborhood used on the HQA visa family page"
      heading="Find out who qualifies as family on an HQA file"
      copy="Not sure whether a spouse or children can be covered? Enter your details and our advisory team can help point you in the right direction."
    />

    <div class="bg-background-alt">
      <div class="site-container py-24 md:py-32">
        <section class="mt-0">
          <h2>Pages in this cluster</h2>
          <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
            <a
              href="/portugal-hqa-visa-spouse"
              class="card cluster-card flex h-full flex-col p-8 transition-[transform,box-shadow,border-color] duration-300 ease-out hover:-translate-y-[5px] hover:border-brand hover:shadow-[0_12px_32px_rgba(28,25,23,0.10)]"
            >
              <h3>Spouse</h3>
              <p class="mt-4 flex-1">
                Partner coverage: marriage or other recognized relationship, and what that proof still has to show.
              </p>
              <span class="btn-primary mt-8 w-full gap-2">
                Read spouse coverage
                <span class="cluster-card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
              </span>
            </a>
            <a
              href="/portugal-hqa-visa-children"
              class="card cluster-card flex h-full flex-col p-8 transition-[transform,box-shadow,border-color] duration-300 ease-out hover:-translate-y-[5px] hover:border-brand hover:shadow-[0_12px_32px_rgba(28,25,23,0.10)]"
            >
              <h3>Children</h3>
              <p class="mt-4 flex-1">
                Dependent children: who counts as a child for this permit family, and which dependency tests still apply.
              </p>
              <span class="btn-primary mt-8 w-full gap-2">
                Read children coverage
                <span class="cluster-card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
              </span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </section>

        <div class="mx-auto mt-24 max-w-3xl">
          <section>
            <h2>How family coverage sits next to the program guide</h2>
            <p class="mt-6">
              Costs multiply when more people are on the file. Application biometrics are individual.               After cards are issued, absences and address rules apply to each holder. After family coverage is mapped, later status is
              <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-permanent-residency" class="inline-link">HQA visa permanent residency</a>.
              For the route as a whole, use the
              <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa" class="inline-link">Portugal HQA visa</a>
              guide.
            </p>
          </section>
          <FamilyClusterNav current="/portugal-hqa-visa-family" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="bg-cta-tint">
      <div class="site-container flex flex-col items-start gap-6 py-24 md:py-32">
        <h2 class="max-w-3xl">Map the household against the principal’s host and the current family list</h2>
        <p class="max-w-2xl">
          This page is informational. It is not legal, tax, or immigration advice. Family categories and evidence lists change. An advisor can tell you whether the spouse and children pages both apply to this household.
        </p>
        {/* TODO: no backend yet */}
        <IntakeForm source="/portugal-hqa-visa-family" simple />
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
